From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 22:09:54 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: keep a terminated invocation's quad in its
 subgroup

A fragment shader that declares RequireFullQuadsKHR keeps every invocation of
a quad, helper invocations included, active for the whole shader, so the
ballots taken after an OpTerminateInvocation still have to count the helper
lanes of a quad whose covered fragment has terminated. Metal does not: the
driver lowers the terminate to discard_fragment() followed by a return, and
discard_fragment() retires the whole 2x2 quad once it has taken the quad's
last live fragment, after which its helper lanes stop answering the SIMD group
functions the ballots are built from.

dEQP-VK.reconvergence.terminate_invocation.bit_count fails on that. Its shader
ballots the subgroup, ballots the invocations that are about to terminate,
terminates them and ballots again, and requires the last two counts to add up
to the first. Rendering the same shape over an 8x8 attachment on an Apple7 GPU
under macOS 27.0 (build 26A428) gives a 32-lane subgroup whose ballot starts at
0xffffffff with helpers 0x0e00e000; terminating the even lanes should leave
0xaaaaaaaa but leaves 0xa0aa0aaa, having dropped lanes 13, 15, 25 and 27 - the
helpers of the two quads whose only covered fragment terminated. The same shape
drawn as one fully covering triangle, which has no helper lanes, is exact, and
replacing the terminate with a plain early return keeps every lane, so it is
the discard that retires the quad rather than the early exit.

Give a terminating invocation a sample mask of zero and return instead. It
writes no colour, depth, stencil or memory either way, it stops contributing to
the group operations that follow because it has left the shader, and the quad
keeps a lane inside the shader until the end, so its helpers stay in the SIMD
group. Only a fragment shader that requires full quads and already carries the
sample mask output that the full-quad lowering writes takes the new path; every
other shader keeps discard_fragment().

Covered by kosmickrisp_terminate_full_quads, which reproduces the loss with
MESA_KK_DISABLE_WORKAROUNDS=19.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
